## Argument Reference

The following arguments are supported:

### Required Arguments

* `name` - (Required) A unique name scoped to your account for the cloud.
* `group_id` - (Required) Specifies which Server group this cloud should be assigned to. **Note:** Changing this forces a new resource to be created.
* `tenant_id` - (Required) Specifies which Tenant this cloud should be assigned to. **Note:** Changing this forces a new resource to be created.

### Optional Arguments

#### General Configuration

* `code` - (Optional) Optional code for use with policies.
* `location` - (Optional) Optional location for your cloud.
* `data_center_name` - (Optional) A custom name used to reference the datacenter for the cloud.
* `visibility` - (Optional) The visibility of the cloud. Valid values are `private` and `public`. Defaults to `private`.
* `enabled` - (Optional) Can be used to disable the cloud. Defaults to `true`.
* `labels` - (Optional) Array of label strings, can be used for filtering.
* `external_id` - (Optional) The external id of the cloud.

#### Agent and Provisioning Settings

* `agent_install_mode` - (Optional) The method used to install the Morpheus agent on virtual machines provisioned in the cloud. Valid values are `ssh` and `cloudInit`. Defaults to `cloudInit`.
* `appliance_url` - (Optional) The URL used by workloads provisioned in the cloud for interacting with the Morpheus appliance.
* `auto_recover_power_state` - (Optional) Automatically Power on VMs. Defaults to `false`.
* `import_existing_vms` - (Optional) Whether to import existing virtual machines. Valid values are `off`, `basic`, and `full`.

#### Cost and Guidance Settings

* `costing_mode` - (Optional) Whether to enable costing on the cloud. Valid values are `off`, `costing`, `reservations`, and `full`. Defaults to `off`.
* `guidance_mode` - (Optional) Whether to enable guidance recommendations on the cloud. Valid values are `off` and `manual`. Defaults to `off`.

#### Security Settings

* `security_mode` - (Optional) Host firewall setting, also known as "local firewall". Valid values are `off` and `internal`. Defaults to `off`.

#### Console Settings

* `keyboard_layout` - (Optional) The keyboard layout to use for the console.

#### HVM Cloud Configuration

* `config_hvm` - (Optional) HVM Cloud specific configuration block. This block supports:
  * `certificate_provider` - (Optional) Certificate provider for the HVM cloud.
  * `enable_network_type_selection` - (Optional) Whether to enable the user to select the network interface type during provisioning.

## Attributes Reference

In addition to all arguments above, the following attributes are exported:

* `id` - The ID of the cloud.

## Import

Clouds can be imported using the `id`, e.g.

```bash
terraform import hpe_morpheus_cloud.example 123
```

## Notes

### Cloud Support

Currently, only the HVM cloud configuration is supported. The `config_hvm` block provides HVM-specific configuration options.

### Agent Installation Modes

* `ssh` - The Morpheus agent is installed via SSH connection to the virtual machine.
* `cloudInit` - The Morpheus agent is installed using cloud-init during the VM provisioning process. This is the recommended method for most cloud platforms.

### Costing Modes

* `off` - No costing functionality enabled.
* `costing` - Basic cost tracking enabled.
* `reservations` - Cost tracking with reservation support.
* `full` - Complete costing functionality with all features enabled.

### Import Existing VMs

* `off` - Do not import existing virtual machines.
* `basic` - Import existing VMs with basic information only.
* `full` - Import existing VMs with complete configuration and metadata.

### Security Modes

* `off` - Host firewall is disabled.
* `internal` - Host firewall is enabled for internal network protection.

### Resource Dependencies

Before creating a cloud resource, ensure that:

1. The specified `group_id` exists and is accessible.
2. The specified `tenant_id` exists and the user has appropriate permissions.
3. Any referenced certificate providers in `config_hvm.certificate_provider` are properly configured in Morpheus.
